    {
      "example_num": 1,
      "example_text": "Input: nums = [1,4,3,2]\nOutput: 4\nExplanation: All possible pairings (ignoring the ordering of elements) are:\n1. (1, 4), (2, 3) -> min(1, 4) + min(2, 3) = 1 + 2 = 3\n2. (1, 3), (2, 4) -> min(1, 3) + min(2, 4) = 1 + 2 = 3\n3. (1, 2), (3, 4) -> min(1, 2) + min(3, 4) = 1 + 3 = 4\nSo the maximum possible sum is 4.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "example_num": 2,
      "example_text": "Input: nums = [6,2,6,5,1,2]\nOutput: 9\nExplanation: The optimal pairing is (2, 1), (2, 5), (6, 6). min(2, 1) + min(2, 5) + min(6, 6) = 1 + 2 + 6 = 9.",
      "images": []
    }
  ],
